          "path": "_m/d/n/5/6/chieftains-museum-wp/chieftain-s-museummajor-ridge--1.jpg",
          "filename": "Chieftain's MuseumMajor Ridge Home, Rome, Georgia (f809ca6e-155d-451f-679b-9bfb112630c7).jpg",
          "caption": "Chieftain's Museum/Major Ridge Home, Rome, Georgia\nThe Chieftains tells the story of Major Ridge, the influential Ridge family including prominent son John Ridge, Cherokee history, and the Trail of Tears, as well as subsequent history of the home and region. Eventually, Major Ridge - and others that became known as the \"Treaty Party\" - began to advocate removal as the only option to preserve the Cherokee people. They were leaders in the signing of the 1835 Treaty of New Echota that resulted in Cherokee removal.\nKeywords: historic site; urban; national register of historic places; national historic landmark; nps centennial; media quality",
